 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Webinar Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a webinar landing page?\", \"a\": \"A webinar landing page is a single page that sells one online session and takes registrations for it. It says what the hour covers and when it starts. Behind its short form, each registrant is passed to the platform that runs the webinar.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I build a landing page for a webinar?\", \"a\": \"Start with the headline and the time, then decide which fields the form needs. With Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, you describe the session in a prompt. Emergent builds the page and its registrant table, and connects the form to your webinar platform's API.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are webinar landing page best practices?\", \"a\": \"Most of what works on a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/lead-generation-landing-page'>lead generation landing page</a> applies here. Promise a result in the headline, and convert the start time for each visitor. Keep the form short. Name the host with a photo, then confirm the time again on the screen after sign-up.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a good webinar landing page example?\", \"a\": \"Landing page builders post roundups of webinar pages on their own blogs. When you study the best webinar landing pages among them, check two things: whether the headline promises an outcome, and whether the form fits on one screen.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free webinar landing page template?\", \"a\": \"Design galleries collect webinar layouts worth studying. A webinar landing page template still leaves the join links and reminders for you to set up. Emergent builds from a prompt instead, and its free tier covers building and publishing the page.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a webinar registration landing page?\", \"a\": \"It is the page that exists to take the sign-up: a short form, the session time, and join details sent back by email. Many hosts use the term for the whole webinar page. Others put the pitch on one URL and the form on a second. A form built on Emergent has no response cap, so a session that draws a crowd keeps taking registrations.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an on-demand webinar landing page?\", \"a\": \"It is the page for a recorded session that people watch whenever they like. The form usually stays, since the recording is the reason to register. The running length replaces the date, and a live page can switch to on-demand at its old address once the session is over.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do separate sessions need separate webinar landing pages?\", \"a\": \"Not always. A one-off session gets a page of its own. A recurring demo or a multi-part series can share one page that lists the dates and lets visitors pick, which keeps a single URL in every ad and email.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do webinar landing page examples have in common?\", \"a\": \"Most fit the headline and the whole form on a laptop's first screen. Speaker photos are large enough to recognize a face. The sign-up button gets the one strong color on the page, and the form is as quick to fill in on a phone as on a desktop.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a webinar get its own website or a single landing page?\", \"a\": \"One page covers a single session or a recurring demo. A program with a back catalog of recordings outgrows it and needs a small site, with an index of past sessions and a replay page for each. On Emergent, both can run on your own domain; custom domains are included and use credits. Pair either with a thank you page that confirms the seat.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
